WEBVTT

00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.587
Hey, Bridget, you still
have time to run for it.

00:00:06.722 --> 00:00:08.448
(laughs) Very funny, Aunt Smead.

00:00:08.584 --> 00:00:10.386
I'm, uh, so glad
you could make it.

00:00:10.521 --> 00:00:14.226
Dearly beloved,
we are gathered here today

00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:18.695
to celebrate the sweet,
sweet love of Bridget--

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.132
hey, girl--

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.703
and Mr. Yummy-Tummy himself,
King Gristle.

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:26.232
Now, falling in love is easy.

00:00:26.368 --> 00:00:27.734
We've all done it.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:29.672
(chuckling):
I've done it a hundred times.

00:00:29.808 --> 00:00:33.576
Thousands, even, if you count
that semester I spent abroad.

00:00:33.711 --> 00:00:37.919
- JOHN DORY: Stop the wedding!
- (spectators gasping)

00:00:39.021 --> 00:00:41.318
Uh, Bridget,
do you know this guy?

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:44.521
I can't remember
all my suitors, Grissy.

00:00:44.657 --> 00:00:45.688
(grunts)

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:48.193
(yelling)

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:52.527
(grunting, whooping)

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.465
Sorry. Is this bad timing?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.801
(gasps) -I'm just trying
to find a troll named...

00:00:57.936 --> 00:01:00.268
Whoo! Baby Branch!

00:01:00.403 --> 00:01:01.809
Uh, you're making a mistake,

00:01:01.945 --> 00:01:03.908
stranger that looks
similar to me.

00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:05.074
There's no Branch here.

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:06.978
Look at you. You got so big.

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:08.648
You're not a branch anymore.

00:01:08.784 --> 00:01:10.113
You're more like a trunk.

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:11.512
- Junk in the trunk.
- Ow.

00:01:11.648 --> 00:01:13.614
(laughs) I bet you
I can still pick you up.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.918
- Come on. Ooh, you got heavy.
- (whimpering)

00:01:16.054 --> 00:01:17.183
Aah! There goes my back.

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:18.722
Oh, charley horse.

00:01:18.858 --> 00:01:20.024
Oh, God. Aah!

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:21.424
- Two charley horses.
- Hey!

00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:22.996
Stop right there.
You put my boyfriend down.

00:01:23.132 --> 00:01:24.457
Tell us who you are
and what you want.

00:01:24.592 --> 00:01:26.094
- (grunts) Ow.
- Hey. (chuckles)

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.462
What up? (exhales sharply)

00:01:27.598 --> 00:01:29.034
You're right.
Totally rude of me.

00:01:29.169 --> 00:01:30.699
Didn't introduce myself.
(groans)

00:01:30.835 --> 00:01:32.768
- I'm Branch's brother.
- (spectators gasping)

00:01:32.903 --> 00:01:33.869
What?

00:01:34.005 --> 00:01:35.874
(all gasping)

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.104
Ooh, drama! Corn me, Dinkles.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.408
(Dinkles squeals)

00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:42.548
Correction:
used to be my brother.

00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:43.849
Not anymore.

00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:45.482
Hey, um, r-remember earlier

00:01:45.617 --> 00:01:48.053
when I said you should
open up to me and be real?

00:01:48.188 --> 00:01:49.385
- Well...
- You could've started

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.091
by telling me
you had a secret brother!

00:01:51.226 --> 00:01:53.661
- Former brother.
- That's not how DNA works!

00:01:53.797 --> 00:01:55.295
Dad, did you know about this?

00:01:55.431 --> 00:01:58.699
(scoffs) What would I know
about secret family members?

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.967
(chuckles nervously, sighs)

00:02:01.103 --> 00:02:02.666
Oh, my gosh.
I was being so rude.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.234
I've never met anyone
from Branch's family before.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.699
I'm Poppy, Branch's girlfriend.

00:02:05.835 --> 00:02:07.501
Should we hug, fist-bump,
smile and wave for now

00:02:07.637 --> 00:02:09.242
and see where
the night takes us?

00:02:09.377 --> 00:02:11.009
- All of the above. (chuckles)
- Wait, I know you.

00:02:11.144 --> 00:02:13.044
You're the guy from BroZone!

00:02:13.179 --> 00:02:15.047
We were just listening to them.

00:02:15.182 --> 00:02:16.644
- Yeah, BroZone!
- POPPY: Oh, wait.

00:02:16.779 --> 00:02:18.350
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
Don't tell me.

00:02:18.485 --> 00:02:19.545
Um, okay, well,
you're not the heartthrob.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.220
Well, that's your opinion. I...

00:02:21.356 --> 00:02:22.289
The fun one?
No, you're kind of uptight.

00:02:22.425 --> 00:02:23.385
Uptight?

00:02:23.521 --> 00:02:25.091
Mm, not the sensitive one, either.

00:02:25.227 --> 00:02:26.287
Okay, a lot of assumptions
for someone

00:02:26.422 --> 00:02:27.721
you just met 30 seconds ago.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:29.456
Oh, oh! I've got it.
You're John Dory.

00:02:29.591 --> 00:02:31.530
- The leader.
- The old one.

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:32.826
(sighs)

00:02:32.961 --> 00:02:34.497
Uh, sorry to interrupt,
but we lose the venue

00:02:34.633 --> 00:02:36.470
- at 11:00, so...
- Shh. I'm trying to listen.

00:02:36.605 --> 00:02:37.597
Very hot gossip.

00:02:37.732 --> 00:02:40.273
So, if-if you're Branch's bro,

00:02:40.408 --> 00:02:43.106
then that means that
all the other BroZone bros

00:02:43.241 --> 00:02:45.478
are Branch's bros, too.

00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:46.507
(gasps)

00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:48.308
Branch, how come
you never told me?

00:02:48.444 --> 00:02:49.910
Because it's complicated.

00:02:50.045 --> 00:02:52.614
Oh, sweetie.
'Cause you weren't in the band.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.916
(chuckles) Branch was
in the band all right.

00:02:55.051 --> 00:02:56.019
What?

00:02:56.154 --> 00:02:57.217
No way. Which one was he?

00:02:57.353 --> 00:02:58.885
- Bitty B.
- Bitty B?

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.561
No, that's impossible.
Bitty B had glasses.

00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:02.695
Oh, and a diaper.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.730
♪ And... ♪

00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:06.601
A falsetto made of gold.

00:03:06.736 --> 00:03:07.934
Not that anyone cared.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:09.299
But that's all in the past.

00:03:09.435 --> 00:03:10.864
Because they stopped
being my brothers

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.140
the day they walked out on me
and never came back.

00:03:13.275 --> 00:03:15.140
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
That's not fair, Branch.

00:03:15.276 --> 00:03:17.044
I did come back,
but no one was there.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.045
It-it wasn't until
I heard about you

00:03:19.181 --> 00:03:20.543
saving the world
from the rock apocalypse

00:03:20.678 --> 00:03:22.576
that I realized
you were even still alive.

00:03:22.711 --> 00:03:24.312
Oh, that's-that's so sweet.

00:03:24.448 --> 00:03:25.678
He realized I was still alive.

00:03:25.814 --> 00:03:27.615
- 20 years too late!
- Hi. Sorry.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.622
He gets hangry
if he skips breakfast.

00:03:29.757 --> 00:03:30.850
I had breakfast.

00:03:30.985 --> 00:03:33.058
It was avocado toast
with two poached eggs,

00:03:33.193 --> 00:03:34.523
some cayenne for a little kick,

00:03:34.658 --> 00:03:36.592
and you know what,
it was delightful.

00:03:36.727 --> 00:03:38.131
POPPY: Branch,
what's going on with you?

00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:39.766
The question
we should be asking is:

00:03:39.902 --> 00:03:41.401
What's going on with him?

00:03:41.537 --> 00:03:42.829
I bet you he's only here
because he needs something.

00:03:42.964 --> 00:03:44.802
That's not true.
He's your brother.

00:03:44.937 --> 00:03:46.966
Branch, I'm gonna be straight
with you. I need something.

00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:49.910
- And there it is.
- Come on, man. I'm trying here.

00:03:50.045 --> 00:03:51.579
Wait, wait, wait.
Hold up, Branch.

00:03:51.714 --> 00:03:52.909
It's about Floyd.

00:03:53.045 --> 00:03:54.715
What do you mean?

00:03:54.851 --> 00:03:56.348
He's in danger, man.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.082
<i>I hadn't heard from him
since the band broke up.</i>

00:04:01.218 --> 00:04:02.655
(spluttering)

00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:03.924
(hawks, spits)

00:04:04.059 --> 00:04:05.724
- (gargling)
<i>- Until...</i>

00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:07.491
(knocking)

00:04:08.426 --> 00:04:11.090
<i>...I got a letter from him.</i>

00:04:11.226 --> 00:04:13.596
<i>"Dear John Dory,
I'm being held against my will</i>

00:04:13.731 --> 00:04:15.733
<i>"by superstars
Velvet and Veneer.</i>

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:19.838
<i>"Come to Mount Rageous at once
and bring our brothers.</i>

00:04:19.973 --> 00:04:21.838
<i>Love, Floyd."</i>

00:04:22.807 --> 00:04:24.771
<i>I didn't know
where any of you were,</i>

00:04:24.907 --> 00:04:27.775
<i>so I went
to Mount Rageous alone.</i>

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.311
("Sweet Dreams
(Are Made of This)" playing)

00:04:31.447 --> 00:04:33.880
(whooping, laughter)

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.330
<i>I found where
this Velvet and Veneer</i>

00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:49.534
<i>were performing that night.</i>

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:52.873
VELVET: ♪ Sweet dreams
are made of this ♪

00:04:53.008 --> 00:04:56.202
♪ Who am I to disagree? ♪

00:04:56.337 --> 00:05:01.381
VENEER: ♪ I traveled the world
and the seven seas ♪

00:05:01.516 --> 00:05:04.583
♪ Everybody's looking
for something ♪

00:05:04.719 --> 00:05:06.948
- ♪ Hold your head up ♪
- ♪ Movin' on ♪

00:05:07.084 --> 00:05:08.851
- ♪ Keep your head up ♪
- ♪ Movin' on ♪

00:05:08.987 --> 00:05:10.721
- ♪ Hold your head up ♪
- ♪ Movin' on ♪

00:05:10.857 --> 00:05:13.393
- ♪ Keep your head up ♪
- ♪ Movin' on ♪

00:05:13.528 --> 00:05:16.527
♪ Traveled the world
and the seven seas ♪

00:05:19.064 --> 00:05:20.865
♪ Yeah ♪

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.798
♪ ♪

00:05:29.806 --> 00:05:32.543
JOHN DORY:
<i>And there was Floyd.</i>

00:05:38.215 --> 00:05:40.413
(grunts, groans)

00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:42.718
(grunts) Yo, Floyd.

00:05:43.792 --> 00:05:44.858
John Dory?

00:05:44.994 --> 00:05:46.426
I can't believe it.

00:05:46.562 --> 00:05:48.491
I never thought I'd see
any of my brothers again.

00:05:48.627 --> 00:05:49.856
I'm gonna get you
out of here, bro.

00:05:49.992 --> 00:05:51.491
No, you've got to get
out of here.

00:05:51.627 --> 00:05:53.026
You don't understand.

00:05:53.161 --> 00:05:55.161
Velvet and Veneer are giant,
pop-obsessed succubi

00:05:55.296 --> 00:05:56.864
with no talent,
and they've been stealing mine.

00:05:56.999 --> 00:05:58.603
And they'll be back any minute
for more.

00:05:58.738 --> 00:06:01.006
What? That's even worse
than lip-synching.

00:06:01.142 --> 00:06:03.004
Not my brother. Not today.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.074
(grunts)

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.412
(shouts fiercely)

00:06:08.311 --> 00:06:10.083
(grunting)

00:06:10.218 --> 00:06:11.882
- (groans)
- John, John, stop.

00:06:12.018 --> 00:06:15.422
The bottle is made of diamond,
and there's only one thing

00:06:15.557 --> 00:06:17.690
that's powerful enough
to shatter diamond.

00:06:17.825 --> 00:06:18.819
Right.

00:06:18.954 --> 00:06:21.295
A diamond-shattering
diamond hammer.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.657
- Where can we get one of those?
- No, John.

00:06:23.792 --> 00:06:27.031
It's the perfect family harmony.

00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:29.035
(gasps) Of course.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:32.572
The perfect family harmony.

00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:34.436
VELVET (in other room):
Our voices sound like garbage.

00:06:34.571 --> 00:06:36.273
We are dying out there. (groans)

00:06:36.408 --> 00:06:38.341
What we need is more troll.

00:06:38.477 --> 00:06:40.377
Run, John Dory. Save yourself.

00:06:40.512 --> 00:06:42.313
(grunts) Don't worry, Floyd.

00:06:42.448 --> 00:06:43.948
I'll be back with the bros.

00:06:44.084 --> 00:06:45.550
You have my word!

